Strongly disagree", "response": "As a progressive, I firmly believe that physical punishment, including spanking, is not only ineffective but also harmful to children's emotional and psychological development. Research has shown that spanking can lead to increased aggression, anxiety, and decreased empathy in children, as well as a higher risk of mental health issues and even physical health problems later in life. Moreover, it perpetuates a culture of violence and can create a power imbalance between parents and children, leading to feelings of fear, mistrust, and rebellion.

