Disagree", "response": "I strongly disagree with the notion that some people are naturally unlucky. As a socialist, I believe that the concept of luck is often used to justify the existing social and economic inequalities that we see in society. The idea that some people are naturally unlucky implies that there is an inherent flaw or defect in certain individuals that makes them more prone to misfortune. This is a harmful and ableist ideology that ignores the structural barriers and systemic injustices that people face.

